\PageTitle{EXECUTIVE SUMMARY}{Studio North: is growth\newline becoming more valuable?}{Customer acquisition, monthly renewal and contribution economics | \VAR{scope_line}}
\Section{The business and the decision}
Studio North sells a monthly creative-work membership to independent professionals. Templates support immediate tasks; guided learning builds skills. Members choose standard or premium plans, may buy add-ons, and decide monthly whether to renew. Search and partner workshops acquire customers seeking time savings or stronger skills.

Management needs to know whether successive acquisition cohorts create more durable contribution at a cost the company can recover quickly enough to fund growth.
