\Section{Operating implication}
The operating review benefits from both the common-age economics of each joining cohort and the company's accumulated contribution. A favorable acquisition metric can coexist with slower cash recovery when renewals weaken. A growing customer base can also conceal deterioration if management replaces departing customers with increasingly costly new ones.
\Boundary{Cash payback is undiscounted: the first age at which cumulative contribution covers the acquisition investment. The LTV calculation that follows discounts expected monthly contribution and uses a common, explicit horizon.}

