\Section{Feature transformations and interpretation}
Mean-churn coefficients use a logit link; concentration and revenue use log links. Search and save-time customers are the reference groups. Retention cohort trend is $(\text{index}-11.5)/11.5$; revenue cohort trend is $(\text{index}-11.5)/12$. Revenue log-age is $\log(1+\text{age})$. Cohort index runs from 0 to 23. A coefficient therefore needs its link, scale and reference group before it has a managerial interpretation.
